  "_about": "Ticket 21, Product Filtering's store-wide default list (PUT /v3/settings/search/filters): Fly Sizes first and open, 15 values, sorted by option value (hook order once ticket 18's Fly Sizes job lands); Category hidden; Brand and Price stay hidden; every other filter keeps the values read on 2026-10-06, with the read-only facet fields left out. The order: Fly Sizes, then the other shown filters in the read's order (Other, Rating), then the hidden ones in the read's order. So Rating moves from 5th to 3rd only because the hidden Category, Brand and Price move below it; on a page, Other and Rating keep their order after Fly Sizes. items_to_show is sent as the string BigCommerce's Update Enabled Filters documents (\"5\", \"10\", \"15\"), though the store reads it back as a number. The list takes no channel_id, so it is Shaun's: plan.mjs --approved, then apply.mjs --approved at his terminal. Who it reaches: contextual filters apply to category pages only (BigCommerce's Contextual Filters guide); brand and search-results pages always use this default list. Channels 1 and 1855224 each have a channel-wide context (category_id 0), so their category pages keep their own lists. But their brand and search-results pages use this list: on reelflies.ca and reelflies.com those pages lose the Category facet, and Fly Sizes moves first with 15 values by option value. ReelFlies_CA (1895766, no context) gets it on every page. The same-day checks (plan/approvals/21-product-filtering.md) read the lists again and check a category, a search-results and a brand page on both live sites.",
